{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":34.900001525878906,"text":"In 1939, in a field in eastern England, an archaeologist and a gardener dug into a mound and found the imprint of a ship 27 meters long. The wood had melted into the soil, but the nails stayed in place, and in the middle lay the treasure of a 7th century king. The helmet was found in hundreds of pieces and was put together twice. It has an iron face with eyebrows, a mustache, and a nose, and if you look at it from the The eyebrows and the nose make a flying dragon. Beside it stands a gleaming replica, so you can see how it shone when new.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.46000000834465027},{"word":"1939","start":0.46000000834465027,"end":1.5199999809265137},{"word":"in","start":1.7599999904632568,"end":1.8600000143051147},{"word":"a","start":1.8600000143051147,"end":2.240000009536743},{"word":"field","start":2.240000009536743,"end":2.240000009536743},{"word":"in","start":2.240000009536743,"end":2.4800000190734863},{"word":"eastern","start":2.4800000190734863,"end":2.7799999713897705},{"word":"England","start":2.7799999713897705,"end":3.1600000858306885},{"word":"an","start":3.640000104904175,"end":3.8399999141693115},{"word":"archaeologist","start":3.8399999141693115,"end":4.440000057220459},{"word":"and","start":4.440000057220459,"end":4.71999979019165},{"word":"a","start":4.71999979019165,"end":5},{"word":"gardener","start":5,"end":5.480000019073486},{"word":"dug","start":5.480000019073486,"end":5.619999885559082},{"word":"into","start":5.619999885559082,"end":5.940000057220459},{"word":"a","start":5.940000057220459,"end":6.380000114440918},{"word":"mound","start":6.380000114440918,"end":6.380000114440918},{"word":"and","start":6.380000114440918,"end":6.940000057220459},{"word":"found","start":6.940000057220459,"end":7.119999885559082},{"word":"the","start":7.119999885559082,"end":7.539999961853027},{"word":"imprint","start":7.539999961853027,"end":7.659999847412109},{"word":"o